import static io.restassured.RestAssured.*; // for Http methods
import static io.restassured.matcher.RestAssuredMatchers.*; //validate REST Assured responses using REST Assured matchers.
import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.*;//Provides Hamcrest matchers used for assertions/validation.

============================================================
        REST ASSURED — IMPORTANT STATIC IMPORTS
============================================================

1. import static io.restassured.RestAssured.*;

PURPOSE:
--------
Used for REST Assured request methods.

It allows us to directly use:

    given()
    when()
    then()
    get()
    post()
    put()
    delete()
    baseURI

Without writing:

    RestAssured.given()
    RestAssured.when()
    RestAssured.get()


EXAMPLE:
--------

given()
    .header("Authorization", "Bearer " + token)
    .body(requestBody)
.when()
    .post(url)
.then()
    .statusCode(201);


------------------------------------------------------------

2. import static io.restassured.matcher.RestAssuredMatchers.*;

PURPOSE:
--------
Provides REST Assured specific matchers.

Used when we need to validate REST Assured responses using REST Assured matchers.
using REST Assured matchers.

Example:

    body("response", someRestAssuredMatcher);


NOTE:
-----
This import is NOT required for every REST Assured test.

If you are not using any RestAssuredMatchers,
you can remove this import.


------------------------------------------------------------

3. import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.*;

PURPOSE:
--------
Provides Hamcrest matchers used for assertions/validation.

Common matchers:

    equalTo()
    not()
    hasItem()
    hasItems()
    containsString()
    startsWith()
    endsWith()
    greaterThan()
    lessThan()
    nullValue()


EXAMPLE:
--------

.then()
    .statusCode(200)
    .body("name", equalTo("Sameer"));


Here:

    equalTo("Sameer")

comes from:

    org.hamcrest.Matchers.*


------------------------------------------------------------

QUICK MEMORY TABLE
------------------------------------------------------------

IMPORT                              PURPOSE
------------------------------------------------------------

RestAssured.*
        ↓
given(), when(), then(), get(),
post(), put(), delete()

        → Used to BUILD and SEND API requests


RestAssuredMatchers.*
        ↓
REST Assured-specific matchers

        → Used for REST Assured-specific validation


org.hamcrest.Matchers.*
        ↓
equalTo(), hasItem(), containsString(),
greaterThan(), etc.

        → Used for RESPONSE ASSERTIONS / VALIDATION


------------------------------------------------------------
EASY WAY TO REMEMBER
------------------------------------------------------------

RestAssured.*
      ↓
REQUEST

RestAssuredMatchers.*
      ↓
REST ASSURED MATCHERS

Hamcrest Matchers.*
      ↓
ASSERTIONS / VALIDATION


IMPORTANT:
----------

You don't necessarily need all 3 imports in every test.

For your current POST test, if you only use:

    given()
    when()
    post()

you mainly need:

    import static io.restassured.RestAssured.*;

If you later add:

    .then()
    .statusCode(201)
    .body("name", equalTo("Sameer"));

then you need:

    import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.*;

